  "body": "## Summary\n\n- exposes exact runtime-gated labels for PlaceToPay card/bank/DeUna and PayPhone wallet without changing legacy Datafast, PayPal, or manual-bank labels\n- adds a shared hosted-provider checkout and `/pagos/retorno` recovery surface for event tickets, courses, bookings, Domo deposits, and mixing/mastering orders\n- persists a tab-scoped marker before provider transmission and reuses only the same provider, method, checkout, and idempotency key after an interrupted create\n- locks every alternate legacy or hosted rail while a result is pending, ambiguous, non-retryable, or successful; only authoritative no-charge releases fallback\n- refreshes the domain order after server-verified success instead of treating a browser return as payment or fulfillment evidence\n- updates OpenAPI and generated web/mobile contracts; mobile paid tickets continue to use the canonical web handoff from diegueins680/TDF-mobile#78\n\n## Dependency and review order\n\n1. #331 \u2014 canonical core, migrations, routing, research, and operations UI\n2. #332 \u2014 PlaceToPay/PayPhone durable backend execution and reconciliation\n3. **this PR** \u2014 exact client capabilities, checkout surfaces, and interruption recovery\n4. diegueins680/TDF-mobile#78 \u2014 mobile paid-ticket canonical handoff/generated contract\n\nBase branch: `codex/payment-provider-execution-20260913` (#332). Do not rebase this directly onto `main` before its dependencies merge.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `cd tdf-hq && stack test --fast --test-arguments='--match provider'` \u2014 77 examples, 0 failures; local compiled unit/property tests with mocked provider boundaries\n- focused Jest command covering capability, session API, return recovery, hosted component, and event integration \u2014 6 suites, 23 tests, 0 failures\n- `cd tdf-hq-ui && npm run typecheck` \u2014 passed\n- `cd tdf-hq-ui && npm run lint` \u2014 passed with zero warnings\n- `cd tdf-hq-ui && npm run build` \u2014 passed; Vite production build and initial-JS budget (378,243 gzip bytes)\n- web and mobile OpenAPI generation reproduced the committed generated types with no diff\n- mobile commit `90a08f56fcd8df08dac2effd9253bceeb2c3e9a8` \u2014 `npm run typecheck` passed in the mobile worktree\n- `npm run test:catalog-list-audit && npm run audit:catalog-lists` \u2014 passed across 1,411 tracked files and 1,122 candidates with zero unreviewed or stale decisions after the nine changed payment-client lists were individually governed\n- `npm test --workspace=tdf-hq-ui -- --runInBand src/features/featureRegistry.test.ts` at `3b81b6877` \u2014 10 tests, 0 failures; confirms `/pagos/retorno` is registered as a non-navigable technical route\n- hosted [CI run `34883596896`](https://github.com/diegueins680/tdf-app/actions/runs/34883596896) at `3b81b6877` \u2014 passed the aggregate quality gate, backend, UI, mobile, repository, API-contract, production-migration, persona E2E, clean-install, catalog-authority, Datadog build, Vercel, and Cloudflare checks; backend additionally passed the disposable merch runtime, automatic-migration, and public-booking concurrency steps\n\nCorrective evidence is retained: the initial focused test exposed an invalid `.rejects` assertion for a synchronous validator and was repaired; one mistyped Jest `--run` invocation did not execute tests; one manual changed-file lint command explicitly included an ignored generated file and exited on that warning. The first hosted catalog-authority run also rejected nine new fingerprints and one stale predecessor; commit `b7896d652` records each exact client mirror/validator against its database or state-machine authority. Hosted run `34877455178` then passed 210/211 UI suites and 1,886/1,887 tests, failing only because `/pagos/retorno` was absent from the canonical feature registry; commit `3b81b6877` repairs that exact assertion. A local full `quality:ui` retry passed lint and typecheck but was stopped after the pre-existing `MarketplacePage` suite produced 5-second timing failures and overlapping-`act()` warnings; its isolated retry reproduced 9 failures/1 pass on this machine, while the same suite passed in both clean hosted runs. Final hosted run `34883596896` is the authoritative full-suite verification and completed successfully.\n\n## Security and migration notes\n\n- no PAN, CVV, provider credential, or provider payload is stored in the client\n- lookup tokens remain in validated tab-scoped storage, never URLs; all return paths are same-origin relative paths\n- PlaceToPay redirects accept HTTPS with no credentials/port and only the exact Ecuador test/production hosts\n- provider success is trusted only from the durable server session; ambiguous create results cannot fall back to another provider\n- the service storefront response adds a nullable canonical checkout UUID; no destructive database migration or historical reinterpretation is introduced here\n\n## Activation blockers\n\n- no TDF merchant contract, sandbox credentials, method/site IDs, registered webhook URLs, controlled PayPhone test users, or provider settlement evidence was available\n- no provider sandbox, staging deployment, live transaction, settlement, or production action was performed\n- all new routes remain invisible until exact account, contract, environment, method, flow, capability, runtime-secret, and worker gates are enabled\n- recurring mandates, saved-card deletion, payment-link execution, authorization/capture/void/refund for the new providers, settlement imports, disputes, and marketplace connected-account/split/payout execution remain separate blocked work\n- marketplace and merchandise were not given a synthetic custody/split mechanism; marketplace activation still requires a provider-approved Ecuador contract plus legal/accounting review\n\n## Review focus\n\n- pre-response and post-response interruption behavior\n- alternate-rail safety lock and authoritative no-charge release\n- exact backend labels vs. OpenAPI/client enums\n- order refresh without direct fulfillment mutation\n- lookup-token and redirect handling\n\nResearch, threat model, rollout, rollback, operator evidence, exact local test boundaries, and the CI corrective record are updated in `docs/payments/` through commit `b7896d652`; the route-governance repair is commit `3b81b6877`.\n",
